  </figure>
  <p>Both aim at the same thing: questions that are easy to ask and easy to trust, about data that stays where it lives. If they work, the slow first question stops being the price of entry, and the approach becomes the ordinary way to do research across organizations rather than the careful exception it is today.</p>
